    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Percentage of youth indicating higher levels of trust towards other ethnic groups: Higher compared to baseline (2023)
1.1.1 At least 420 young people from different ethnic communities who take part in adventure and fun activities and engage in inter-cultural interaction along the Via Dinarica trails. (2023)
1.1.2 At least 150 young people from different ethnic communities who take part in the Via Dinarica Youth Games Without Borders.(2023)
1.2.1 At least 150 young people engaged in volunteer initiatives together with peers from different ethnic groups. (2023)
1.2.2 Increased level of awareness after the delivery of the learning and awareness raising events; (2023).
1.3.1 The first national tourism school award scheme is developed (2023)
1.3.2 At least 50 young people who successfully gather seals from the Via Dinarica school award scheme (2023)
2. Higher extent of support among young people on cooperation and dialogue between different ethnic groups; (2023).
2.1.1 At least 2 national TED Youth Talks organised by 2021 and at least 20 young leaders (male and female) present their stories. (2023).
2.1.2 At least 100 young people who improve critical thinking and leadership skills and apply them in their communities to bridge social divides. (2023)
2.2.1 At least 1 National Youth Innovation Challenge organised by 2021 and at least 150 young people from different ethnic backgrounds take part; (2023).
2.2.2 At least 20 innovative ideas / solutions generated by young people during the challenge.</narrative>
    </description>
